        "note": "Visible boundary of the short-mown, striped fairway against the paler rough, followed by eye on the native 0.16 m panel (a global contrast stretch and a smoothness/excess-green false-colour rendering of the same pixels were viewing aids only; no classification was adopted). Runs from the diagonally striped approach between the two greenside bunkers, overlapping the front of the putting surface rather than asserting a boundary through it, down to the rounded forward end above the tee path. The two left-side fairway bunkers, the right-side bunker and the left greenside bunker stay outside on their own mown collars. Replaces the club-plan reading, which spanned the rough to the treeline; the OSM strips once assigned here (w284933769, w284933770) are the short course's 4th and 5th.",
